id: pm-swarm-close-warning-receipt
title: Recover native dependency warnings after an interrupted close
description: "Swarm now preserves all native close warnings when available and reports warnings_unavailable with an explicit inspect-dependent-items remedy when the SDK interrupted before its close result checkpoint. Native item and history recovery still converges without duplicate closes. The pinned public CommitWorkspaceTransactionOptions.onTransition contract defines step_applied after mutation and before journal recording; PmClient.close returns ephemeral warnings, and commitItemMutations delegates to the same coordinator lock. No public native-close result receipt API can recover those warnings at that boundary. Upstream issue search found no open matching warning-receipt issue. Follow up when the SDK durably records the native result before that interruption boundary; retain the conservative availability signal for legacy journals."
type: Issue
status: blocked
priority: 2
tags[2]: durability,sdk-gap
created_at: "2026-10-27T14:32:22.495Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T16:39:02.223Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-swarm-y972
blocked_reason: Pinned SDK exposes step_applied before persisting the native result and exports no durable native-close warning receipt; an upstream SDK change is needed.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T16:25:46.348Z",codex-agent,"Round 6: the same public WorkspaceTransactionStep.apply result boundary also governs secondary ownership receipts. The SDK persists results after step_applied, so a process loss before recording can lose native dependent receipts as well as warnings. Pre-admitted secondary heads are now journaled before native close; recovery refuses compensation when those advanced and ownership cannot be proven, preserving native state instead of reopening only its blocker. Exact durable receipts, when recorded, compensate every owned dependent and resume without duplicate restores. See docs/native-close.md and test/close-compound-effects.test.ts."
